  "dcterms:title": "PubMed / MEDLINE citation baseline (NCBI/NLM)",
  "dcterms:description": "A BioBricks brick named 'pubmed' built from the NCBI/NLM PubMed annual baseline XML files (pubmed25, ~38.2M records) downloaded from the NCBI FTP server, parsed into a partitioned Parquet dataset with extracted columns (PMID, Title, Abstract, DOI, Year, Authors, Journal, MeSH_Terms, Keywords, Pub_Types, dates, and the full JSON record). The upstream source is PubMed, produced by the US National Library of Medicine (NLM) at NIH. PubMed citation metadata is a US government work, but individual abstract texts are frequently authored/owned by third-party publishers and carry their own copyright.",
