  "biobricks:reviewed": false,
  "biobricks:reviewNotes": "Determined by the annotation agent (Claude, slice items[1350:1356]). The brick downloads the NCBI/NLM PubMed baseline (confirmed by stages_v2 and README). PubMed *citation metadata* (PMIDs, titles, MeSH, journal, dates) is a US government work and effectively public domain, BUT the brick materially includes the full Abstract text of each article, and NLM/NCBI state that abstracts and other content may be protected by third-party (publisher/author) copyright. Under the 'most restrictive component governs' rule, the presence of copyrighted abstract text means the dataset-as-a-whole is restricted / license-required (Schedule A Lr); it is classed 'unknown' here rather than 'restricted' only because NLM's custom Terms and Conditions are not a standard license IRI the validator recognizes, and the precise combined redistribution terms are genuinely undetermined. Commercial redistribution is conservatively marked prohibited because no blanket right to redistribute the copyrighted abstracts is granted. HUMAN REVIEW REQUIRED: NLM's PubMed/MEDLINE download Terms and Conditions permit broad reuse (including commercial) of the *metadata* with attribution and no-endorsement conditions; if the abstract column were excluded or its third-party status accepted, a reviewer could downgrade this to attribution/conditional. Verify the exact NLM Terms and Conditions text at https://www.nlm.nih.gov/databases/download/terms_and_conditions.html.",
